    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0532" n="444" xml:id="pg444"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/949: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wheeler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-02T11:00:00-04:00">February 2, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. Your circular telegram of February 1, 7 p.m. See the last paragraph of my
                    telegram No. 16 of January 28, 2 p.m.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d428-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d428-f1" n="75" xml:id="d428-f1-content">
                <p>It read: “At Brazil’s request Paraguay today telegraphed Peru urging her to
                    accept Brazil’s proposal, already accepted by Colombia, to the effect that Peru
                    retire all Peruvians from Leticia after which Brazil will return the territory
                    to Colombia as a preliminary to a reconsideration of the treaty.”
                    (724.3415/2837)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
